  {
    "sha": "b3a68d63d1b2a6174b23ab78ec068345a7df526f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGIzYTY4ZDYzZDFiMmE2MTc0YjIzYWI3OGVjMDY4MzQ1YTdkZjUyNmY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T01:23:41Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T01:23:41Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(3d): rapid to the plunge height before a pocket restart, merge sub-resolution feeds\n\nA 3D Pocket pass that restarts after a hop with a straight plunge now\ngoes down by a rapid to the plunge height over the material, then\nfeeds the rest (descent::feed_down, as a level entry does). Before, it\nfed the whole way from the hop plane.\n\nThe finished 3D Pocket path merges each straight feed that moves less\nthan 0.001 mm on every axis into its straight neighbour. Such a move\nposted as a G01 with the same X, Y and Z as the block before it.\n\nThe catalog case 3d/rough-finish is made again: 28 sub-resolution\nG01 lines leave the 3D Pocket section.\n\nFixes #3852\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "69aa51aa5c75cb5c578a102f19a29d7b6ff5a02b",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/69aa51aa5c75cb5c578a102f19a29d7b6ff5a02b"
